          "source_quote": "Μαρόνην τὸν ἀποδεξάμενον αὐτόν, ἤδη λοιπὸν τέλειον ὄντα",
          "english_quote": "Maron, who had received him and was by now mature",
          "issue": "“Mature” is a defensible contextual rendering of τέλειον, but its significant status ambiguity is not disclosed. Besides spiritual or moral maturity, “complete” or “perfected,” potentially referring to completed initiation in this baptismal context, is a material alternative. The draft's notes do not explain why maturity is selected.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a lexical note quoting “ἤδη λοιπὸν τέλειον ὄντα,” explaining the contextual maturity reading and preserving “now complete/perfected,” potentially “fully initiated,” as an alternative. Do not present initiation as an explicit or uniquely established meaning. The main rendering need not be rejected merely because these alternatives exist; the revised disclosure must undergo fresh review.",
